## Run order (development)

<%
// One hint per stack × recorded build system; refs without one
// (manifests predating the per-service choice) read the default.
const runHints = {
  'quarkus-rest': {
    gradle: './gradlew quarkusDev',
    maven: './mvnw -am -pl application/rest/executable quarkus:dev',
  },
  'spring-rest': {
    gradle: 'SPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE=dev ./gradlew bootRun',
    maven: 'SPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE=dev ./mvnw -am -pl application/rest/executable spring-boot:run',
  },
  'micronaut-rest': {
    gradle: 'MICRONAUT_ENVIRONMENTS=dev ./gradlew run',
    maven: 'MICRONAUT_ENVIRONMENTS=dev ./mvnw -am -pl application/rest/executable mn:run',
  },
  'go-http': { default: 'GO_ENV=dev go run ./cmd/http' },
  'rust-http': { default: 'cargo run' },
  'ts-http': { npm: 'npm run dev:rest', pnpm: 'pnpm run dev:rest' },
  'web-components': { npm: 'npm run dev', pnpm: 'pnpm run dev' },
};
const runHint = (service) => {
  const hints = runHints[service.stack];
  if (!hints) return 'see its README';
  return hints[service.buildSystem] ?? hints.default ?? Object.values(hints)[0];
};
const backendService = services[0];
const frontendService = services[services.length - 1];
-%>
1. Start the backend first:
   ```sh
   cd <%= backendService.path %> && <%= runHint(backendService) %>   # serves http://localhost:8080
   ```
2. Then the frontend dev server:
   ```sh
   cd <%= frontendService.path %> && <%= runHint(frontendService) %>   # proxies /api → localhost:8080
   ```

The frontend reaches the backend through its `gateway-rest` driven
port; in development Vite proxies `/api`, in production set
`VITE_API_BASE_URL` at build time (12-factor: config via env). The
wire itself is pinned by the backend's
[`contract/greet.openapi.yaml`](<%= backendService.path %>/contract/greet.openapi.yaml).

The backend's CORS accommodation for the Vite origin (for calling
the API directly, without the `/api` proxy) is **dev-only** — the
run commands above activate it where the stack needs a flag — and is
never served in production, where SPA traffic arrives same-origin
through the frontend's reverse proxy.

## Run containerised

```sh
docker compose up --build   # SPA on http://localhost:8081, /api proxied to the backend
```

One image per deployment unit, built from the Dockerfile beside it.

## Working here

Each service is independently buildable and testable — see its own
README. Changes that cross services (e.g. the greet contract) land as
one commit in this repository.
